  "note_on_attribution": "Credits are per artefact and were rewritten twice (2026-11-01, 2026-11-03) to remove a third-party project name; git history was squashed at the same time, so per-file authorship no longer exists. What the record can still show: who wrote the migration that touched a file last (#34, 58 adapters), and who is credited for the artefact. A credit that looks wrong should be corrected here, in one line, and the drawings follow.",
  "attribution": "Benchmarks are credited to whoever proposed the dataset, not to whoever touched it last: the PRs that introduced the adapter decide, and a later migration (#34 changed every adapter's storage contract) does not move the credit. Where no PR introduced an adapter it predates the pull-request history and is credited to the catalogue's author."
